    "per_pillar_md": {
      "P1": "Bell Bank articulates a digital strategy with executive sponsorship and targeted cloud investments [E-100, E-101, E-102], yet implementation remains hampered by siloed governance structures, limited innovation capacity, and inconsistent culture change mechanisms. The bank scores 2.05/5 (0.70 points below peer median 2.75), signaling need for tighter strategy alignment and scaled innovation governance.",
      "P2": "Bell Bank delivers competitive omnichannel and direct digital experiences [E-500, E-501] but lacks the customer data infrastructure required for segment-level personalization at scale. The bank scores 2.09/5 overall in customer experience, outperforming on delivery channels (2.22/5 omnichannel, above median) but severely constrained in personalization (2.38/5 driven by basic alerts and no life-event detection). A customer data platform is the critical blocker for P2 advancement.",
      "P3": "Bell Bank maintains strong operational resilience [E-714] and fraud prevention [E-607, E-608] but remains dependent on manual processing and legacy middleware. The bank scores 2.15/5, at peer median in compliance and fraud, and above peer median in resilience (2.50/5), but constrained by process automation (1.94/5, at peer median). Infrastructure modernization is critical to unlock operational efficiency gains.",
      "P4": "Bell Bank's technology stack is fragmented across legacy core platforms and modern cloud services, creating data silos and limiting analytics maturity [E-801, E-803]. The bank scores 1.77/5 (below peer median 2.00), with critical gaps in data governance (1.69/5, -0.31), analytics (1.75/5, -0.25), and technology architecture (1.79/5, -0.71). Data governance is foundational to unlock personalization, advanced analytics, and AI-driven operations."
    },
